# Project Phoenix - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
Autonomous AI Agent for Shiprocket Frontend. Self-healing: fix production errors, reduce tech debt, raise PRs.
7 repos: legacy AngularJS to modern Angular 17+.

## Coding Standards (Phoenix Agent)
- Python 3.11+ with type hints
- Use TypedDict for state; keep nodes pure (return dict updates)
- Config in YAML (.yaml), secrets in .env
- Brain: Opus 4.6 (claude-opus-4-6)

## Architecture
- LangGraph nodes in src/orchestrator/nodes/
- One concern per node; shared state via PhoenixState
- Services (repo, github, validator) in src/services/
- Analyzer in src/analyzer/ for repo diagnostics
- No business logic in main.py; only CLI and invoke

## Shiprocket Angular Standards (apply when editing target repos)
- Always use SCSS for styles (not CSS, Less)
- Follow Clean Architecture: feature modules, lazy loading, shared module
- Use Signals for state in Angular 17+
- Migrate legacy AngularJS patterns to modern Angular where feasible
- ng test + ng lint must pass before PR
